A proposed alternative to the current Qt/GTK2/Win32 graphical 
interfaces:

# SVG (scalable vector graphics) icons replacing tiles - searching on 
Google groups revealed no prior discussion of vector graphics on rgrn. 
SVG graphics scale with resolution and size and when compressed should 
have a smaller filesize than large tiles. Icons intended to be easily 
recognisable, memorable and attractive - not realistic in proportion or 
perspective.

# Different icon sets. Prototype to use SVG coloured ASCII characters, 
which can be kept as an amusing retro option. Define a default set, and 
let users specify additional (perhaps incomplete) icon sets which 
overrule default icons and previous custom sets in order specified.

# Possibly simple in-place animations for tiles - not action animations, 
but animations that loop. Improves looks, and should help clarity - e.g. 
only monsters animate, different members of the same group animate 
differently.

# Could also include indicators of sleeping/trapped/peaceful/scared 
statuses of monsters through extra icons or animations

# Drag-and-drop items. For example, drag a potion from main inventory to 
a container to stash it, a Quaff icon to drink it or a direction icon to 
throw it. Drag polearms, appropriate spells, Jump command onto map 
square to include target in command. For other icons dragging to map 
counts as nearest 8-way direction, highlighting direction under cursor.

# Highlight icons and map squares under cursor, only when they can be 
clicked/dragged onto, to avoid clicking mistakes. Red border? 
Highlighting arrows also highlights squares in that direction on map and 
vice versa.

# Tooltips on icons. Tooltip on map square gives info on square, 
including sleep/scared etc statuses of monsters.

# Effects of LMB/MMB on map squares redefinable, RMB gives menu (e.g. 
movement/info)

# Change appearance of direction arrows according to whether they move 
character or complete command - e.g. try to prevent kicking item off 
trap whilst leg is hurt and moving onto it

# Item menu windows have tools to select/deselect/toggle each of 
all/type/B/C/U/regexp so can for example select armour and then deselect 
cursed, leaving B/U armour items only.

# Maintain (most) current key commands - may need to be adjusted to 
reflect item selection system.

Windowing system probably Qt4, targetting all FLOSS Qt platforms - Win, 
Linux, MacOS X.

